   "label": "About this template",
   "s": {
    "text": "A control interaction, a subsynchronous oscillation or a badly tuned loop shows up as an oscillation that does not decay. Start the damping window after the disturbance itself, so its own step is not read as a peak. A negative damping ratio means the oscillation is growing."
   },
   "pin": [],
   "sv": 1
  },
